    "q-174362": {
      "dom_id": "step-q174362",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nA=\\{x\\in R∣{x}^{2}=4\\},\\,B=\\{x\\in R∣{x}^{2}<-1\\}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A=\\{2\\}$\n\nII. $A\\cap B=∅$\n\nIII. $A$ and $B$ are disjoint",
      "worked_solution": "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the elements of $A$ are the real numbers that satisfy the equality\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\ |x| & =2 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Statement I is false.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\{x\\in R∣{x}^{2}=4\\} \\\\  & =\\{-2,2\\} \\\\  & \\ne \\{2\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\{x\\in R∣{x}^{2}<-1\\} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the intersection is \n\n$$\nA\\cap B=\\{-2,2\\}\\cap ∅=∅.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the intersection is empty, the two sets are disjoint.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
