    "q-174364": {
      "dom_id": "step-q174364",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nA=\\{{n}^{2}∣n\\in N\\},\\,B=\\{\\frac{2}{n}∣n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A=\\{1,4,9,16,…\\}$\n\nII. $A\\cap B=∅$\n\nIII. $A$ and $B$ are disjoint",
      "worked_solution": "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Statement I is true.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\{{n}^{2}∣n\\in N\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,4,9,16,…\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\{\\frac{2}{n}∣n\\in N\\} \\\\  & =\\{2,1,\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2},…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the intersection is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cap B & =\\{1,4,9,16,…\\}\\text{ }\\cap \\{2,1,\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2},…\\} \\\\  & =\\{1\\}. \\\\  & \\ne ∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the intersection is not empty, the two sets are not disjoint.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
