    "q-172542": {
      "dom_id": "step-q172542",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nA=\\{n\\in Z∣3n-8<7\\},\\,B=\\{n\\in Z∣n\\ge 5\\}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A=\\{…,3,4,5\\}$\n\nII. $A\\cap B=∅$\n\nIII. $A$ and $B$ are disjoint",
      "worked_solution": "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the elements of $A$ are integers that satisfy the inequality \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n-8 & <7 \\\\ 3n & <15 \\\\ n & <5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Statement I is false.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\{n\\in Z∣3n-8<7\\} \\\\  & =\\{n\\in Z∣n<5\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,2,3,4\\} \\\\  & \\ne \\{…,3,4,5\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\{n\\in Z∣n\\ge 5\\} \\\\  & =\\{5,6,7,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the intersection is \n\n$$\nA\\cap B=\\{…,2,3,4\\}\\cap \\{5,6,7,…\\}=∅.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the intersection is empty, the two sets are disjoint.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
