    "q-174424": {
      "dom_id": "step-q174424",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Find the disjoint union of the sets ${A}_{1}=\\{-2,\\pi \\}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\{\\pi ,4\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the sets are overlapping since\n\n$$\n\\{-2,\\pi \\}\\cap \\{\\pi ,4\\}=\\{\\pi \\}\\ne ∅.\n$$\n\nSo, for each of our sets, we form the associated set, where each element is tagged with the corresponding index, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {A}_{1} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{1}^{∗}=\\{(-2,1),(\\pi ,1)\\} \\\\  & {A}_{2} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{2}^{∗}=\\{(\\pi ,2),(4,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the disjoint union of our sets is simply the union of the associated tagged sets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2} & =\\{-2,\\pi \\}⊔\\{\\pi ,4\\} \\\\  & ={A}_{1}^{∗}\\cup {A}_{2}^{∗} \\\\  & =\\{(-2,1),(\\pi ,1)\\}\\cup \\{(\\pi ,2),(4,2)\\} \\\\  & =\\{(-2,1),(\\pi ,1),(\\pi ,2),(4,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
