    "q-174444": {
      "dom_id": "step-q174444",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Find the disjoint union of the sets ${A}_{1}=\\{a,b,c\\}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\{b,c,d\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the sets are overlapping since\n\n$$\n\\{a,b,c\\}\\cap \\{b,c,d\\}=\\{b,c\\}\\ne ∅.\n$$\n\nSo, for each of our sets, we form the associated set, where each element is tagged with the corresponding index, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {A}_{1} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{1}^{∗}=\\{(a,1),(b,1),(c,1)\\} \\\\  & {A}_{2} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{2}^{∗}=\\{(b,2),(c,2),(d,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the disjoint union of our sets is simply the union of the associated tagged sets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2} & =\\{a,b,c\\}⊔\\{b,c,d\\} \\\\  & ={A}_{1}^{∗}\\cup {A}_{2}^{∗} \\\\  & =\\{(a,1),(b,1),(c,1)\\}\\cup \\{(b,2),(c,2),(d,2)\\} \\\\  & =\\{(a,1),(b,1),(c,1),(b,2),(c,2),(d,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-174444-a",
